{
  "dom_id": "step-q5057",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "An office typist was given the task to transfer all the work documents to the company's internal system. The following table shows some statistics on the process.\n\n| **$t\\,\\text{(hour)}$** | $4\\text{th}$ | $5\\text{th}$ | $6\\text{th}$ | $7\\text{th}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${D}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{(documents/hour)}$ | $11$ | $8$ | $7$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThe typist transfers the documents at a rate of ${D}^{′}(t)$, where ${D}^{′}(t)$ is measured in documents per hour. At the end of the seventh hour, $t=7$, the typist had completed $50$ documents. Use the tangent line approximation of $D$ at time $t=7$ to determine the number of documents transferred after the ninth hour.",
  "worked_solution": "The tangent line approximation of $D(t)$ at the point $a=7$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(t) & =D(a)+{D}^{′}(a)(t-a) \\\\  & =D(7)+{D}^{′}(7)(t-7) \\\\  & =50+10(t-7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $D(9)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $t=9.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(9) & ≈L(9) \\\\  & =50+10(9-7) \\\\  & =50+10(2) \\\\  & =50+20 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
